{{also|vùo|vüö}}
==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|eo|pl|wu}}, chosen for being similar to {{l|eo|kuo||Q}}.

Coined by Sergio Pokrovskij in ''Komputika Leksikono'' in 1995 as a less ambiguous alternative to the more common names {{l|eo|duobla vo}} (which can be taken to mean "vv") and {{l|eo|vavo}} (which can also be used for the Hebrew letter [[vav]] or the Arabic letter [[waw]]).

